\f1\fs22 At around four-thirty on Christmas morning, his device woke him, hailing him as said king of said world, and wrenching him  from a lovely dream. \'93What the tax?\'94\
\'93It\'92s Dr Ortolan,\'94 Dr Ortolan said, as even-tempered as ever.\
\'93Really? I thought it was Santa\'92s elves confirming they\'92d delivered my Nobel Peace Prize to the stocking on my mantelpiece.\'94\
\'93For your lifelong commitment to team morale? I think it\'92s still in internal mail.\'94\
\'93Don\'92t be a smart-dick, Ortolan.\'94\
\'93Sorry. I\'92d thought you\'92d want to know\'85 someone\'92s downloaded a software upgrade to the Washing Machine.\'94\
\'93What? Well it wasn\'92t me.\'94\
\'93Yes, well, you are not exactly software are you?\'94\
\'93Software is for minions, Ortolan. Dispensable, replaceable, like cogs in an atomic clock.\'94\
Ortolan took a breath. \'93You\'92d better get down here.\'94\
